    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But that's just it, though. The idea of \"another symphony\" feels like a lie I tell myself to keep going. It's not about a new chapter, it's about the fact that the book is finished. I can feel the exhaustion in my bones. There's a certain dignity in knowing when the work is complete, isn't there? To just... step away while the music is still beautiful, rather than letting it turn into a messy, stumbling imitation of what it used to be.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
